 "coverage_note": "This historical row keeps its published v1.5 headline. Its language and category cells come from a new measurement on the current item pools (S+P, L1, L2, L3), run with the original pinned model and serving setup on an isolated machine; each item was sent once and failed requests stay scored as failures. About 1,000 issued items were lost to out-of-memory kills and a machine shutdown; they stay counted as spent and are never re-asked, so 17 of 23 languages rest on 50 to 59 answered items instead of the 60-item target. Headline, rank, Composite and pricing are unchanged. L3 items were reviewed by an OpenAI model, so cells based on L3 carry that exposure; headline scores do not use L3.",
